I've confirmed the RefCell panic:

```rust
if let Some(selected) = work.context.selected_photo.borrow().as_ref().cloned()
{
    selected.set_edit_recipe(recipe.clone());
    work.context.selected_photo.replace(Some(selected));  // PANIC: borrow() still held by if-let
```

In Rust 2021, the temporary from `if let` scrutinee lives for the entire if-let block. `RefCell::replace` calls `borrow_mut` → panic "already mutably borrowed".

Also in finish_bulk_recipe:
```rust
if let Some(selected) = work.context.selected_photo.borrow().as_ref().cloned() {
    work.context.info.set_photo(Some(&selected));  // set_photo might re-enter selected_photo?
}
```
If set_photo doesn't touch selected_photo RefCell, OK. But if info.set_photo triggers something that writes selected_photo... Looking at infobar set_photo - probably doesn't. Still safer to clone first.

Fix both. Also extract selected photo clone properly:

```rust
let selected = work.context.selected_photo.borrow().as_ref().cloned();
if let Some(selected) = selected {
    if let Some((_, recipe)) = updates.iter().find(|(id, _)| *id == selected.id()) {
        let recipe = recipe.clone();
        selected.set_edit_recipe(recipe);
        work.context.selected_photo.replace(Some(selected));
        work.touched_selected = true;
    }
}
```

For bug3: "add the export to the top right button" - Add an Export button in the top-right header (right_header), wired to the same handler as info.export.

Looking at toolbar.rs - header_tools is packed to right_header with sort and settings. layout.rs packs add_selected_to_collage. build.rs packs stop_scan.

Best approach: create an export button in build.rs, pack it to right_header (or into header_tools). Since header_tools is in toolbar.rs and built separately, and export handler is in build.rs where we have gallery/selection - I should create the header export button in build.rs near stop_scan, pack_end to right_header.

But pack_end order: later pack_end is more to the left in GTK (pack_end packs from the end). stop_scan is pack_end at 2883. If I pack_end export after, export appears to the left of stop_scan. header_tools also pack_end.

Actually in AdwHeaderBar, pack_end widgets: first packed is rightmost. toolbar packs header_tools (sort+settings) - those end up rightmost if packed first... Order of calls matters across functions. configure_toolbar is probably called before or after build section.

Simplest: extract the export click logic into a shared function/slot, and connect BOTH info.export and a new header button to it.

Looking at how info.export handler is set up - I'll refactor to a closure `export_clicked: Rc<dyn Fn()>` that both buttons use.

