Several issues:
1. Done button not found - maybe editor still open but Done name is different, or AT-SPI cache issue. Need to re-search.
2. uinput write fails with EINVAL - the input_event struct size/packing might be wrong. On 64-bit Linux, struct input_event is:
```c
struct input_event {
    struct timeval time; // 16 bytes on 64-bit (2x long)
    __u16 type;
    __u16 code;
    __s32 value;
};
```
My ctypes Structure has `time` as `c_long` which is 8 bytes, but timeval is 16 bytes (timeval = 2 longs: tv_sec, tv_usec)!

That's the bug - need timeval of2 longs = 16 bytes.

Also Done button - maybe after set_text the tree is stale. Let me re-find Done.

